  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1127 AM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nAs temperatures heat up, the UL ridge will begin to flatten over the \nsoutheast. This allows some unsettled weather to enter the area \nstarting on Saturday morning and continuing into the next work week. \nThe rain amounts look decent so far, but there is still a lot of \ndisagreement on amounts in the guidance so that will likely shift. \nMost likely period for heaviest rainfall right now looks to be \nSaturday night into Sunday morning, with another disturbance coming \nin on Monday. \n\nTemperatures will stabilize in the mid 70s for highs, \nbut continue warming into the mid to upper 50s for overnight lows\nthrough the forecast period.",
